      "correctOptionId": "69112187",
      "independentSolution": "Electric energy density has dimensions energy/volume = ML^-1 T^-2. Therefore a=1, b=-1, c=-2 and 2a-b+c=1. Independent cross-check: ε₀ from Coulomb’s law has Q²/(force length²), E has force/Q; multiplying yields force/area = ML^-1 T^-2.",
